gcrig 1  mesh:/Game/GraphCodeExamples/RifleWalk_20261003/SM_RifleManBody  into:/Game/__MCPTests/Gait_20261007/Runner
         faces:+Y  mirror:false  stance:t_pose  binds:tight  influences:8
         body_speed:400  body_accel:850
# body_speed / body_accel (MOVE-ROOT1 R7, Docs/GC-MOVE-ROOT-STATE-PLAN.md "R7 END TARGET", 2026-10-12): 400 cm/s is this rig's
# source subject's measured run (Hamner, 3.96 m/s; Docs/Research/human-running-gait.md). body_accel bounds the body's horizontal
# acceleration at every support knot, an instantaneous bound, so it is the PEAK of maximal braking, -850 +/- 107 cm/s^2, not its
# whole-stop mean -445 +/- 61 that this line first held (Harper et al., Docs/Research/body-momentum-references.md). User 2026-10-12:
# "Raise it as you wish". Measured on native9's exact body-state inputs (Saved/Research/MoveTimingMethod/root-state-independent-v001/
# leg-recovery-v001/cap-sweep): the drawn strides ask mean 415-985 cm/s^2 per stance; at 450 the capped body ran 47 cm behind and
# 26 cm under RunKick's drawing at the kick, at 850 26 cm and 13 cm, ordinary strides within 7 cm / 3 cm, no clip worse.
# MOVE-GAIT1 G4/G5 TEST RIG (Docs/GC-MOVE-GAIT-PLAN.md), a copy of RifleWalk_20261003/RifleMan.gcrig built into __MCPTests:
# the same joints and skin, with the ranges a walking and running person uses (codex's cited curves,
# Docs/Research/gait-reference-curves.md): the ankle plantarflexes to 50 (RifleMan stops at 10; a walk's push-off needs 17,
# a run's 23-31), the thighs and the three spine joints twist (RifleMan locks both; a walk turns the hip -13..+6 and the
# trunk counter-turns 13-21), and the feet carry heel, ball and toe contacts on their own bones for plant(..., roll=).
# Proven here first; RifleMan gets the same ranges once the run and the full-body walk are accepted.

# THE RIFLE WALKER'S RIG (user, 2026-10-03: "choose any one even if it's not rig, then rig it. I don't want you
# to waste anymore time hard coding things"). Epic's tutorial mannequin (SK_RifleMan, a copy) REBUILT as a rig: its
# joints stay where Epic put them and keep their names, every bone now points down its limb and bends where its
# region says, so a .gcmove says axis=fold, a contact by name and a grip, never a raw bone axis or sign. The
# keep-the-skin route was tried first and refused: a region there re-aims an imported bone, which is not built.
#
# Joint places: gc_read kind:"rig" of the same import (SK_LowSwing). Creases, pads and soles: the closing side of
# each joint on the skin and the pads SwordContacts.gcrig measured, in reference component space (faces +Y, up +Z,
# its left +X). Ranges are pairs with zero straight. Written by make_rig.py from those numbers.
#
# influences:8 (2026-10-05, Docs/GC-MOVE-ARM-LADDER.md rung 3): the fewest the twist spread allows. At 12 the voxel
# bind kept about 0.5% of each finger's skin on fingers two away, and once one fingertip rested on a held part, the
# collision fit refused every other finger's step for that tip's skin; the support hand on a staff stayed open.
build {
  SK_Runner = skeletal_mesh()
  IKR_Runner   = ik_rig() [iterations=200]
  # gives= is how far a held thing may press into the skin, in cm, as VRHand.gcrig says it (0.35): with none, the
  # rifle grab refused fingers resting 0.001 to 0.3 cm into the gun.
  PHAT_Runner  = physics_asset() [bodies=hull, gives=0.35]
}
